278	\title{So Below: Empirical Exploration of the Universal Imscriptive Grammar}
279	
280	\author{Lando Mills \\ \normalsize Independent Researcher}
281	\date{\today}
282	
283	\maketitle
284	
285	\emph{v0.2.1 --- 2026-06-18}
286	
287	\begin{center}
288	\rule{0.5\textwidth}{0.4pt}
289	\end{center}
290	
291	\begin{abstract}
292	We introduce the \emph{Universal Imscriptive Grammar} (\UIG): a twelve-primitive
293	grammar assigning any system a coordinate in a discrete space of
294	17,280,000 types --- the \emph{Crystal of Types}. Induced from the
295	scientific literature as the minimal shared properties of recognition events, the
296	twelve primitives are independently confirmed by a companion categorical derivation
297	(\emph{As Above}). The derivations are Frobenius duals ($\mu \circ \delta = \text{id}$):
298	this paper is the $\mu$ half. A central theorem, mechanised and universally
299	quantified, establishes \emph{Frobenius non-synthesizability}: a \emph{single}
300	sub-Frobenius component suffices to deny $\Ppms$ to a composition of any size,
301	so no accumulation strategy reaches it. The grammar encodes itself at address
302	6,734,591 in the $\Oinf$ tier of the Crystal it derives.
303	
304	Validated across over 5,000 imscribed systems: the inflationary epoch and high-dose
305	5-MeO-DMT dissolution imscribe to identical tuples ($d = 0.000$); the Riemann
306	Hypothesis is a completeness question about $\Ppms$ on the critical line; a two-gate
307	consciousness score predicts $C = 0.677$ for magnetars, $C = 0$ for black holes and
308	white dwarfs; the Liar paradox requires $P = \Ppms$ --- dialetheia is structurally
309	necessary. The grammar identified the SIC-POVM obstruction as a $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$-gap
310	that no accumulation of pairwise checks can close, and named descent from the
311	arithmetic object as the only route past it; that prediction has since been
312	executed, and existence at $d = 12$ is a machine-checked theorem obtained by
313	exactly that route. The full catalog is released as open-source software.
314	\end{abstract}\begin{center}
315	\rule{0.5\textwidth}{0.4pt}
316	\end{center}
317	
318	\noindent\textbf{Keywords:} Universal Imscriptive Grammar; types;
319	Crystal of Types; self-modeling; criticality; Frobenius algebra;
320	cross-domain classification; consciousness score; dialetheia;
321	paraconsistent logic; Graham Priest; true contradiction
322	
323	\newpage
324	
325	% ============================================================
326	\section{Introduction}
327	\label{sec:intro}
328	
329	The grammar wasn't designed. It was induced. We call the resulting
330	framework the \emph{Universal Imscriptive Grammar} (\UIG). The name is earned,
331	not chosen: the Crystal of Types has a tier boundary (determined
332	entirely by four gate primitives: $\text{{\igprimfont ⊣}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⊙}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⊤}}$) that
333	encodes the full inner structure of the Crystal
334	(the remaining 43,200 inner types per tier cell). The boundary encodes
335	the bulk --- the definition of imscriptive. The framework is a type
336	theory because it assigns structural universals, not ontological
337	descriptions: two systems sharing the same tuple are \emph{co-typed},
338	not identical.
339	
340	The cross-domain results in \Cref{sec:applications} are structurally
341	unfamiliar, and the imscribing protocol in \Cref{sec:methods} is the
342	primary entry point: assigning a tuple to any well-understood system
343	grounds the coordinates before the unfamiliar identifications are
344	encountered. We note one structural asymmetry that governs how the
345	paper reads: the framework encodes the process of understanding it.
346	A reader who has worked through the imscribing protocol occupies a
347	different structural position from one who has encountered the
348	results descriptively --- the directed distance from the endpoint
349	back to the starting state is $d_\to = 1.0$; in the forward
350	direction, $d_\to = 16.3$~\cite{juster1961}. The distinction is
351	not rhetorical. It is a consequence of the $\OmegaZtwo$ winding
352	the framework assigns to any system whose coordinates have been
353	actively encoded: they can be falsified, but they can't simply
354	dissipate.
355	
356	The origin was a pair of prompts about supramolecular chemistry. The
357	first asked for a survey of imscriptions --- recognition motifs that appear
358	in crystal engineering, retrosynthetic analysis, and self-assembled
359	architectures. The second asked: given everything the literature
360	already knows about imscriptions across all these domains, what do they
361	have in common? What is the minimal set of properties that every
362	recognition event, regardless of substrate or scale, actually shares?
363	
364	The initial response wasn't the grammar. It was a partial, chemistry-dominant
365	set of properties --- overlapping, with some structural dimensions fused and
366	others absent. That response was raw material, not the answer. What the
367	language model surfaced was a chemistry-native vocabulary with the right
368	shape but the wrong resolution: some properties subsumed others, topological
369	protection was absent, kinetics and chirality were conflated under a single
370	temporal label. The twelve-primitive grammar emerged from applying formal
371	independence and completeness tests to that raw material: orthogonality tests
372	to eliminate redundant dimensions, diagonalization tests to reveal missing
373	axes, and logical delamination to separate enfolded predicates
374	(see \Cref{sec:methods}, \S\,Origin).
375	
376	The trapdoor was not a chemistry term. It was $\text{{\igprimfont ∋}}$ (Composition). Composition is dangerous
377	because it immediately raises its dual: decomposition. Once you ask how a thing is composed,
378	you must ask what a thing is, where its boundary lies, and how that boundary persists under change.
379	A synthon is already a partially detached object --- neither fully independent nor fully embedded,
380	defined through its capacity for future coupling and past disconnection. The moment composition
381	is made scale-independent, the question is no longer chemical. It is ontological. Topology
382	(how things connect), chirality (how histories matter), winding (how structures recur),
383	criticality (whether the loop closes on itself) --- these are not additional features bolted onto
384	composition. They are what composition requires once scale is removed as a constraint. The remaining
385	eleven primitives precipitate out of $\text{{\igprimfont ∋}}$ by logical necessity. The grammar was not
386	invented from that prompt. It was drawn out.
387	
388	This inversion of direction is characteristic of the grammar's derivation generally. Standard
389	development is synthetic and bottom-up: declare primitives, define operations, build upward.
390	Characterizing a Totality proceeds in the reverse direction. The Totality already contains
391	everything by definition; it cannot be built, only uncovered. The grammar was not
392	reached by adding structure where there was none. It was reached by removing the noise
393	--- formal independence tests, diagonalization, delamination --- until the underlying geometry
394	became visible. The process could have stopped at any number of primitives. It stopped at twelve
395	because the tests ran out of things to separate.
396	
397	What those tests converged on were twelve questions, each structurally
398	independent of the others. What geometry does the event operate in? How
399	are partners internally connected? What physical mechanism enables binding?
400	Does the system prefer donors, acceptors, or both? How thermodynamically
401	reliable is the interaction? How fast or slow does it equilibrate? At what
402	spatial scale does it coordinate? What logic governs partner selection? Is
403	the system near a critical point? What stoichiometry governs the event? Is
404	the structure topologically protected? Does history matter? Twelve
405	primitives, ordered within each dimension: the grammar was extracted from
406	the literature by a process that could have returned a different number, and
407	didn't.
408	
409	That it didn't return a different number is now confirmed from the opposite
410	direction. A companion derivation (\emph{As Above}) begins not
411	from chemistry but from a single abstract category --- the minimal
412	mathematical object that captures structure and transformation without
413	presupposing elements, order, or metric --- and applies three types of
414	operations: logical (yielding $\text{{\igprimfont ⊙}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⊣}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⊡}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont >}}$, \text{{\igfont 𐑹}},
415	$L_6$), inductive (yielding $\text{{\igprimfont ⊥}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⊡}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⊢}}$, Yoneda/Lawvere), and
416	algebraic (yielding $\text{{\igprimfont ⊞}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⊤}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ⋈}}$, $\text{{\igprimfont ∋}}$). The same twelve
417	primitives emerge, in the same families, with the same value counts.
418	No empirical data was consulted. The two derivations are Frobenius
419	duals of each other in the grammar's own sense: this paper is the
420	$\mu$ half (multiplication --- the grammar acting on specifics and
421	compressing them into tuples), the companion is the $\delta$ half
422	(comultiplication --- one mathematical object unfolding into the
423	full twelve-primitive structure). The Frobenius condition
424	$\mu \circ \delta = \mathrm{id}$ holds at the meta-level: applying
425	the grammar to the grammar's own derivation returns the grammar.
426	
427	The first test wasn't planned. A well-studied benchmark in
428	supramolecular chemistry --- the competitive displacement ordering of
429	guests in CB[7] host-guest systems, where the experimental ranking is
430	known --- was imscribed using only the ordinal rank of the fidelity
431	primitive $\text{{\igprimfont ⋈}}$. The expectation was that a displacement ordering would
432	require at minimum partial binding-energy data; the grammar is
433	structurally coarse-grained, not thermodynamic, and doesn't compute
434	binding affinities. No binding energies, no density functional theory,
435	no solvation models. The algebra predicted the correct competitive
436	displacement ordering six out of six times~\cite{kim2001,assaf2015}.
437	The expectation was wrong. It was the first indication that the grammar
438	was not capturing approximate structural trends but a discrete ordering
439	that binding energy happens to be downstream of --- that something
440	structurally real had been extracted from the literature, not imposed
441	on it.
442	
443	What happened next wasn't planned either. The grammar was extended,
444	one question at a time, to domains it wasn't built for. Hv1 proton
445	channels from organisms separated by 300 million years of evolution
446	imscribed at distance zero: the same constraint structure, different
447	primary sequences, different regulatory mechanisms. The inflationary
448	epoch of the early universe and the high-dose 5-MeO-DMT dissolution
449	state imscribed at distance zero: the same primitive tuple, different
450	scales. The axion and the Higgs boson imscribed at distance zero. Dark
451	matter imscribed outside the Standard Model particle catalog, separated
452	from every known SM particle by conflicts in at least three primitives.
453	The Standard Model and quantum gravity frameworks, imscribed at their shared
454	imscriptive limit, separated by a single architecturally irreducible primitive:
455	the $\text{{\igprimfont ∈}}$-scope gap between renormalizable local continuum (\text{{\igfont 𐑔}}) and
456	imscriptive global structure (\text{{\igfont 𐑲}}). At every extension, the grammar returned results.
457	Most were expected. Some were not.
458	
459	None of these were designed. The grammar didn't predict them; it classified them.
460	The classifications said things the uncoverers had no intention of saying.
461	
462	\begin{figure}[H]
463	\centering
464	\begin{tikzpicture}[
