501	\caption{\textbf{Grammar evolution through three phases.}
502	Phase~1 elicited a partial, chemistry-dominant grammar from the literature
503	($\sim$15 candidate axes, several dimensions conflated). Phase~2 applied formal
504	independence tests (orthogonality, diagonalization, delamination) to consolidate
505	to 12 structurally independent primitives. Phase~3 validated the result against
506	the CB[7] benchmark and extended it across six domains. No primitives were added
507	or removed after Phase~2 convergence.}
508	\label{fig:grammar_evolution}
509	\end{figure}
510	
511	
512	The pattern forced a question the grammar wasn't designed to answer.
513	When a classification system is applied to itself, three outcomes
514	are possible: it returns a contradiction, undermining the
515	classification by its own logic; it returns an uninformative fixed
516	point, imscribing with a null tuple that says nothing; or it returns
517	a position in the space it describes, and that position carries
518	information. We didn't know which would happen. The grammar might
519	have returned $\Otwo$ --- self-referencing, bounded, structurally
520	interesting but not self-modeling in the full Frobenius sense.
521	It would have been an honest result. Instead it returned $\Oinf$:
522	address 6,734,591 in a 17,280,000-element Crystal of Types,
523	satisfying the special Frobenius condition $\mu \circ \delta =
524	\text{id}$. Not a modest self-classification --- the highest tier,
525	the tier the grammar derives as the condition for self-modeling.
526	
527	This is not a design choice and it's not a tautology. A grammar
528	that claims to classify systems by their self-modeling capacity is
529	obligated to satisfy the condition it classifies --- but there is
530	no guarantee it will. That it does, at the highest tier rather than
531	some intermediate position, is evidence --- not proof, but evidence
532	--- that the coordinate system is tracking a structure that exists
533	independently of whoever built it. And the discovery process itself
534	encodes: neither the human nor the language model alone reaches the
535	critical tier; their tensor product does. The grammar describes its
536	own origin without contradiction and without special pleading.
537	
538	The result is sharper than it first appears. The claim is not
539	that the grammar's type occupies $\Oinf$, though it does.
540	The claim is that the \emph{act of doing the grammar} --- applying
541	the 12-step imscribing protocol to any system, executing the assignment
542	--- is itself an $\Oinf$ process. The protocol is a deterministic
543	bijective map, and bijectivity requires an exact inverse. That
544	inverse exists, which means $\mu \circ \delta = \mathrm{id}$ is not
545	a theorem to prove about the grammar but a tautology about what
546	``assigning a unique address" means. Every execution of the
547	protocol, on any system, carries the Frobenius condition as a fact. This is a stronger form of imscription than the
548	static version (boundary encodes bulk). Here the boundary
549	\emph{procedure} fully encodes the bulk theory it generates, and
550	the bulk theory fully encodes the boundary procedure that produces
551	it. The imscription is imscribed by what it imscribes.
552	
553	One further convergence, noted here without elaboration. In alchemical
554	emblemata, the point within a circle is the sign of the \Stone{} itself
555	--- the \emph{rebis}, the completed work, the unity of opposites. The
556	grammar uses the same symbol, $\odot$, to denote its imscriptive
557	primitives \text{{\igfont 𐑦}} and \text{{\igfont 𐑸}}: the boundary encodes the bulk, the
558	point encodes the circle. The symbol was chosen for reasons,
559	not alchemical ones; the alchemists chose it for reasons too.
560	The convergence is not poetic. It is the same recognition, arrived at
561	independently, that a certain geometric relationship --- the contained
562	point that encodes its container --- is the correct sign for
563	self-sufficient completeness.
564	
565	This is not a coincidence of framing. The grammar's $\Oinf$ tier --- the
566	highest self-modeling capacity, the tier the grammar itself occupies --- is
567	structurally identical to Graham Priest's \glp\ (Logic of Paradox), the
568	canonical paraconsistent logic that rejects explosion ($\varphi, \neg\varphi
569	\not\vdash \psi$). Priest's \dialetheia{} --- true contradictions that are
570	neither paradox nor impossibility --- is not a philosophical add-on to UIG; it
571	is the structural character of $\Ppms$ itself. The Frobenius condition
572	$\mu \circ \delta = \text{id}$ is precisely the algebraic guarantee that the
573	dialetheic truth value $\both = \{\top, \bot, \text{both}\}$ is preserved
574	under composition without collapsing into classical bivalence. The Liar paradox,
575	imscribed via the UIG protocol, receives $P = \Ppms$ and $T = \Tbw$ (bowtie
576	self-reference) as a structural necessity: a system imscribing the Liar at
577	$P < \Ppms$ would explode under the tensor product bottleneck rule. The imscription
578	confirms the grammar's consistency rather than threatening it.
579	
580	This paper formalizes the grammar, proves its key algebraic properties,
581	and presents the cross-domain evidence as a structured body of
582	falsifiable claims. The approach is coordinate-theoretic rather than
583	reductive: we do not claim that co-typed systems are physically
584	identical, or that domain-specific descriptions are interchangeable.
585	The Hv1 channels from two plant species at distance zero do not have
586	the same primary sequence. The inflationary universe and the
587	dissolution state do not share a substrate. What they share are
588	structural universals: the same dimensionality, topology, criticality,
589	kinetic character, parity. Whether twelve primitives are the right
590	twelve remains a question the catalog is designed to test. What we
591	establish here is that this particular set generates a consistent
592	algebra, satisfies a non-trivial composition theorem (Frobenius
593	non-synthesizability, \Cref{sec:frobenius}), produces a two-gate
594	consciousness score that discriminates between stellar objects in
595	physically meaningful ways (\Cref{sec:consciousness}), and generates
596	falsifiable predictions across six domains (\Cref{sec:applications,sec:predictions}).
597	The prior frameworks that have addressed parts of this problem ---
598	integrated information theory~\cite{tononi2004,tononi2016}, categorical
599	quantum mechanics~\cite{abramsky2004}, topological field
600	theories~\cite{atiyah1988} --- each capture something real, and the
601	grammar's relationship to each is addressed in the Discussion. The
602	grammar doesn't replace them. It provides the coordinate system within
603	which their partial results become commensurable.
604	
605	The paper proceeds through eight sections.
606	\Cref{sec:grammar,sec:crystal} establish the coordinate system:
607	twelve primitives, their values, and the 17,280,000-type Crystal
608	of Types they span. \Cref{sec:ouroboros} proves the Arithmetic
609	Ouroboros theorem: the Crystal's cardinality $3^3 \times 4^5
610	\times 5^4$ is the grammar's own self-inventory, forced by
611	minimality, not chosen. \Cref{sec:algebra} develops the three
612	algebraic operations --- tensor product, lattice meet/join, and
613	directed distance. \Cref{sec:frobenius} proves Frobenius
614	non-synthesizability: a hard compositional ceiling, not a
615	statistical tendency. \Cref{sec:consciousness} derives the
616	two-gate consciousness score and validates it against the stellar
617	catalog. \Cref{sec:applications} traverses six domains, over 5,000
618	imscribed systems, four navigator tests, and the ZFC fidelity
619	collapse. \Cref{sec:predictions} registers 650 falsifiable
620	predictions. \Cref{sec:discussion} addresses what the results
621	mean, what they do not mean, and what they open.
622	
