736	
737	The choice of twelve primitives is not arbitrary. Each primitive
738	captures a structural universal that is (i)~not reducible to any
739	combination of the others, (ii)~distinguishable by structural
740	arguments alone without reference to specific physical laws, and
741	(iii)~finitely ordered in a manner consistent across domains. The
742	\emph{imscribing protocol} --- the procedure for assigning a tuple to
743	a given system --- is defined in \nameref{sec:methods}. A companion
744	derivation (\emph{As Above}) obtains the same twelve
745	by categorical construction from first principles, independently of
746	the empirical induction described in \Cref{sec:intro}: starting from
747	a single abstract category, three operation types (logical, inductive,
748	algebraic) force the primitive set with no free choices.
749	
750	\paragraph{Selected primitive glosses.}
751	Dimensionality $\text{{\igprimfont ⊢}}$ measures the extent and character of the state
752	space: \text{{\igfont 𐑛}} (wedge, simplest nontrivial extent), \text{{\igfont 𐑨}}
753	(triangulated finite complex), \text{{\igfont 𐑼}} (infinite-dimensional, e.g.\
754	Hilbert space), \text{{\igfont 𐑦}} (imscriptive: boundary imscribes bulk, the
755	monad symbol $\odot$ for point-in-circle; see terminological note below). Topology $\text{{\igprimfont ⊣}}$ encodes
756	connectivity: \text{{\igfont 𐑡}} (flat network), $\Tin$
757	(inward-folded containment), $\Tbw$ (dual-lobe coupling as in
758	color confinement), $\Tbox$ (crossed product, e.g.\ spin
759	networks), \text{{\igfont 𐑸}} (imscriptive closure). Criticality $\text{{\igprimfont ⊙}}$
760	encodes proximity to a critical manifold: $\Phic$ is the
761	critical point itself, the unique locus where self-modeling loops are
762	topologically permitted. Winding $\text{{\igprimfont ⊡}}$ encodes the topological
763	invariant of the system's phase space: \text{{\igfont 𐑷}} (trivial),
764	\text{{\igfont 𐑴}} (binary, e.g.\ time-reversal symmetry),
765	\text{{\igfont 𐑭}} (integer winding, e.g.\ topological insulator),
766	\text{{\igfont 𐑟}} (not applicable, e.g.\ ecosystems without a
767	natural winding class).
768	
769	\paragraph{Terminological note: \emph{imscriptive}.}
770	\label{par:imscriptive}
771	Throughout this paper the adjective \emph{imscriptive} is used in preference
772	to \emph{holographic} to describe the bulk-boundary imscription property
773	realised by \text{{\igfont 𐑦}} and \text{{\igfont 𐑸}}. A system is \emph{imscriptive} if
774	its boundary surface fully encodes all interior degrees of freedom ---
775	so that the bulk is recoverable from boundary data alone, without
776	remainder. The verb is \emph{to imscribe}; the noun is
777	\emph{imscription}. The term is formed from \emph{im-} (Latin, within/immersed;
778	cf.\ \emph{immerse}, \emph{implant}, \emph{imbue}) and \emph{-scriptive}
779	(from L.\ \emph{scribere}, to write): to imscribe is to write the
780	interior into the boundary.
781	
782	\emph{Holographic} is not used for three reasons.
783	(1)~It carries optical connotations from three-dimensional imaging that are
784	irrelevant to the information-theoretic claim being made.
785	(2)~The term has migrated into cognitive science and
786	distributed-representation literature as a loose ``whole-in-part"
787	metaphor, diluting the specific bulk-boundary correspondence to
788	something much coarser.
789	(3)~The optical etymology encodes the wrong direction: an optical
790	hologram stores a diffuse record of a source; imscription specifies
791	that the \emph{boundary writes} the bulk --- a directional claim about
792	imscription, not storage. The distinction matters: imscription is a
793	completeness property (nothing of the bulk escapes the boundary's
794	imscription), while optical holography is a redundancy property (every
795	part of the plate contains enough information to reconstruct the image).
796	These are not the same claim, and the physics literature has paid a
797	price for conflating them.
798	
799	The monad symbol $\odot$ --- a point inscribed within a circle --- is
800	the visual realisation of imscription: the interior (point) written
801	within the boundary (circle). The symbol was chosen independently of
802	the terminology; the convergence is structural.
803	
804	\subsection{The $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$-primitive and dialetheia}
805	\label{sec:p_dialetheia}
806	
807	The parity primitive $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$ has five ordered values. The jump from
808	$\text{{\igfont 𐑯}}$ to $\Ppms$ is not a continuous promotion but a structural
809	phase transition to a different logical tier. $\text{{\igfont 𐑯}}$ systems have
810	exact $\mathbb{Z}_2$ symmetry but cannot consistently encode true
811	contradictions: coupling a system at $\text{{\igfont 𐑯}}$ with its negation
812	via the tensor product bottleneck rule (\Cref{def:bottleneck}) gives
813	$\text{{\igprimfont <}}(X \tensor \neg X) = \text{{\igfont 𐑯}}$, which admits explosion. $\Ppms$
814	systems are different in kind. They satisfy the Frobenius condition
815	$\mu \circ \delta = \text{id}$, which is precisely the algebraic
816	guarantee that the dialetheic truth value $\both = \{\top, \bot,
817	\text{both}\}$ is preserved under composition without collapse.
818	
819	The five $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$-values in ascending order:
820	\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*, label=\arabic*.]
821	  \item $\text{{\igfont 𐑗}}$ --- broken symmetry; no structural constraints.
822	  \item \text{{\igfont 𐑿}} --- complex phase symmetry (exact coherence); \text{{\igfont 𐑐}} required.
823	  \item \text{{\igfont 𐑬}} --- $\mathbb{Z}_2$ parity; classical or quantum.
824	  \item $\text{{\igfont 𐑯}}$ --- exact $\mathbb{Z}_2$ symmetry; full symmetry
825	    but no explosion-free guarantee.
826	  \item $\Ppms$ --- \emph{Frobenius-parity-symmetric}: $\mu \circ \delta
827	    = \text{id}$. This is the structural realization of Graham Priest's
828	    \glp\ explosion-free consistency. Systems at $\Ppms$ can encode
829	    $\both$ without collapse.
830	\end{enumerate}
831	
832	\noindent
833	This is a \TOPO\ claim: it follows from the $\min$ rule on $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$ under
834	tensor product and requires no physical imscription. Its
835	\ONTO\ implication is that any self-referential system --- the Liar
836	paradox, G\"{o}del's incompleteness sentence, UIG itself --- must be
837	at $\Ppms$ to avoid explosion. The Frobenius non-synthesizability theorem
838	(\Cref{sec:frobenius}) proves that $\Ppms$ cannot be reached by composing
839	sub-Frobenius components; the dialetheic tier is not emergent.
840	
