1841	    \label{eq:sic_open} \\[4pt]
1842	  \text{SIC}_\text{proven} &= \langle \text{{\igfont 𐑦}} \text{{\igfont 𐑸}} \text{{\igfont 𐑽}} \Ppms \text{{\igfont 𐑐}} \text{{\igfont 𐑧}} \text{{\igfont 𐑲}} \text{{\igfont 𐑵}} \Phic \text{{\igfont 𐑫}} \text{{\igfont 𐑳}} \text{{\igfont 𐑷}} \rangle
1843	    \label{eq:sic_proven}
1844	\end{align}
1845	
1846	The grammar distance is $d \approx 4.09$, with the dominant contribution at
1847	$\text{{\igprimfont <}}$: from $\Ppm$ (approximate $\mathbb{Z}_2$, as in pairwise equiangularity
1848	checks) to $\Ppms$ (exact Frobenius self-duality, $\mu \circ \delta =
1849	\text{id}$). This is the \emph{Frobenius cliff}. \Cref{thm:frobenius}
1850	explains directly why it resists pairwise proof strategies: $\Ppms$ is
1851	not synthesizable from sub-Frobenius components. No accumulation of
1852	pairwise checks closes the $\text{{\igprimfont <}}$-gap; it must be planted as a primitive. Appleby et al.\ \cite{afmy2017} showed that SIC fiducial
1853	vectors are units in ray class fields $L_d$ over $\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{d(d-2)})$
1854	with palindromic Galois self-duality. The grammar reads that palindromic
1855	condition as $\Ppms$ directly: the Stark unit in $L_d$ is the object
1856	that already inhabits the $\Ppms$ tier, bypassing the Frobenius cliff
1857	by Galois descent rather than equiangularity-by-equiangularity.
