1859	\paragraph{The bypass, executed.}
1860	Since this section was first written the predicted route has been carried out in
1861	the kernel rather than argued for. At $d = 12$ the existence of a SIC-POVM is now
1862	a machine-checked theorem. The proof accumulates no equiangularity checks: it
1863	constructs an existence ring carrying the $d^2 - 1 = 143$ overlap identities,
1864	exhibits a ring homomorphism $\varphi : R \to \mathbb{C}$, and transfers the
1865	identities across it --- descent from the arithmetic object, which is precisely
1866	the route this section predicted and \Cref{thm:frobenius} requires. The proof
1867	depends on no axiom of the project. The same architecture closes the shadow at
1868	$d = 2^{11} = 2048$, where an explicit $\mathbb{C}$ fiducial is produced and the
1869	transport is proof-complete.
1870	
